0_2022_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassAMember_uSpATJM3_kmt9pGpclQ4qQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockParOrStatedValuePerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_5z6fFTxmrU2jdjfk00DnLQ">0.000125</ix:nonFraction> each. As a result, the Company had <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_rpTrCvjq9EKNFIg_LlTg9g" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2022_EKQTD7bx9U6v13TvOjZVmA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockSharesAuthorized" scale="0" id="Narr_lX_XMb_Aike_DUS8nc3NXA">1,600,000,000</ix:nonFraction> authorized shares in total, comprising (i) <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_rpTrCvjq9EKNFIg_LlTg9g" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2022_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassAMember_uSpATJM3_kmt9pGpclQ4qQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockSharesAuthorized" scale="0" id="Narr_5NvDHE84nUeLTV3wOyQYvQ">1,550,000,000</ix:nonFraction> Class A ordinary shares of a par value of US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_IzWs318Ci0mMCjIpiA9Avw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2022_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassAMember_uSpATJM3_kmt9pGpclQ4qQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockParOrStatedValuePerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_fy1ob2HNlkyfXYK5A4uvAw">0.000125</ix:nonFraction> each, (ii) <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_rpTrCvjq9EKNFIg_LlTg9g" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2022_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassBMember_osq9XuvIGEutCHW7TqA-aQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockSharesAuthorized" scale="0" id="Narr_6CRTo-_2-06d3KTmb6vJyQ">50,000,000</ix:nonFraction> Class B ordinary shares of a par value of US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_IzWs318Ci0mMCjIpiA9Avw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2022_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassBMember_osq9XuvIGEutCHW7TqA-aQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockParOrStatedValuePerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_TXughoNumk6lUkNT1KUpDA">0.000125</ix:nonFraction> each.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On May 10, 2024, the Company effected a change in the ratio of our ADSs to Class A ordinary shares from <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_rpTrCvjq9EKNFIg_LlTg9g" contextRef="Duration_3_1_2021_To_3_31_2021_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_dei_AdrMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_IPOMember_mfOvjqIKtE2gapCd3Ecc9w" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="zh:NumberOfAdssRepresentingOneClassOrdinaryShare" scale="0" id="Narr_PMG3fbyZE0CSDcbXzTDfJQ">two</ix:nonFraction> ADSs representing one Class A ordinary share to a new ratio of one ADS representing <span style="-sec-ix-hidden:Hidden_6K5sYYCOvUeDxI4n19ykpA;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">three</span></span> Class A ordinary shares.</p></ix:nonNumeric><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_AJB2peQrjUiqS8bvKhZUFQ" name="us-gaap:DisclosureOfCompensationRelatedCostsShareBasedPaymentsTextBlock" id="Tb_rmPpGhV0Bk-RziustF1XIg" continuedAt="Tb_rmPpGhV0Bk-RziustF1XIg_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">15.&#160;&#160;Share-based Compensation</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In June 2012, the Company established 2012 Incentive Plan, which permits the grant of options, and restricted shares of the Company to relevant directors, officers and other employees of the Company and its affiliates. In June 2022, the maximum number of shares that may be issued under the 2012 incentive compensation plan was <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_rpTrCvjq9EKNFIg_LlTg9g" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2022_us-gaap_PlanNameAxis_zh_IncentiveCompensationPlan2012Member_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassAMember_kv7y0QPYN0CjqBEk0ZVyiQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardNumberOfSharesAuthorized" scale="0" id="Narr_r0BkheTctU-wf9Jd2PGfwA">44,021,165</ix:nonFraction> Class&#160;A ordinary shares.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In June 2022, the Company established 2022 Incentive Plan, which permits the grant of options, and restricted shares of the Company to relevant directors, officers, employees and consultants of the Company and its affiliates. The maximum number of shares that may be issued under the 2022 Incentive Plan is the sum of (i) the maximum of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_rpTrCvjq9EKNFIg_LlTg9g" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2022_us-gaap_AwardTypeAxis_us-gaap_EmployeeStockOptionMember_us-gaap_PlanNameAxis_zh_IncentiveCompensationPlan2022Member_PccGLEcrkUiw6CYiH1dAIA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardNumberOfSharesAuthorized" scale="0" id="Narr_8ox2S42E5EiMyoMSFvQ55Q">13,042,731</ix:nonFraction> shares which may be issued pursuant to awards in the form of options, and (ii) the maximum of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_rpTrCvjq9EKNFIg_LlTg9g" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2022_us-gaap_AwardTypeAxis_us-gaap_RestrictedStockMember_us-gaap_PlanNameAxis_zh_IncentiveCompensationPlan2022Member_BKFdZpwEt0uxaGkjWRmXzg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardNumberOfSharesAuthorized" scale="0" id="Narr_NGR9VVNMikWKIG3QqhrakQ">26,085,463</ix:nonFraction> shares and such number of shares equivalent to the unused portion of the 2012 Incentive Plan as at the expiry of such plan, which may be issued pursuant to awards in the form of restricted shares.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Under the 2012 Incentive Plan, during 2012 and 2013, options or restricted shares granted are subject to both service conditions and the occurrence of an initial public offering (&#8220;IPO&#8221;) as a performance condition, which are measured at the grant date fair value.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">After 2013, participants are granted options or restricted shares which only vest if certain service conditions are met. Participation in the 2012 Incentive Plan is at the board&#8217;s discretion, and no individual has a contractual right to participate in the 2012 Incentive Plan or to receive any guaranteed benefits. Options issued under the 2012 Incentive Plan are valid and effective for <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_AwardTypeAxis_us-gaap_EmployeeStockOptionMember_us-gaap_PlanNameAxis_zh_IncentiveCompensationPlan2012Member_UGX4DEIw80y4ES3V6bt7ag" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="us-gaap:SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardExpirationPeriod" id="Narr_HFAZRGEtpU6d9FratKLDuw">10 years</ix:nonNumeric> from the grant date.</p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-42</p></div></div>
